Frostary - Privacy Policy

Last updated: 26 November 2026

Frostary is a mobile puzzle game made by CodingTech Studio, Başakşehir / İstanbul, Türkiye ("we").
Contact: codingtechstudio@gmail.com

Frostary is made for adults. It is not directed to children and we do not knowingly collect data from children.


1. What stays on your device

Your progress, coins, boosters, collection and settings are stored only on your device. We have no account system and no server of our own. Deleting the game deletes this data.


2. Crash reports

When the game crashes, a crash report is sent to Google Firebase Crashlytics so that we can find and fix the error. A report holds the error trace, the device model, the operating system version, the game version and an installation identifier created by Crashlytics. It does not hold your name, e-mail address, contacts or location. Legal basis: our legitimate interest in keeping the game working.


Game settings: when the game starts it asks Google Firebase Remote Config for balance settings (for example reward amounts and how often ads may appear). The request carries a Firebase installation identifier, the game version, and your language and country setting. It holds nothing about how you play and is not used to treat players differently. Legal basis: our legitimate interest in keeping the game balanced.


3. Play statistics (only if you allow them)

The first time you open the game it asks whether it may collect anonymous play statistics. If you choose "Allow", the game sends events such as "level started", "level completed", "booster used" or "coins spent" to Google Analytics for Firebase, together with an app-instance identifier, coarse device information (model, operating system, language, country) and the time. We use them to see where players get stuck and to balance the levels. Legal basis: your consent.

If you choose "No, thanks", no play statistics are collected or sent, and the game works the same.

You can change your choice at any time under Settings > Privacy options. Choosing "No, thanks" there stops the collection and deletes the analytics data stored on your device. While statistics are allowed, the same window shows your Data ID; you can send it to us to have the statistics linked to it deleted.

The advertising identifier is not used for statistics, and the statistics are not used to personalise ads.


4. Ads

The game shows ads through Google AdMob: videos you choose to watch for a reward, and full-screen ads between some levels. To show and measure ads, Google receives the advertising identifier of your device, your IP address (from which an approximate location is derived), device information and your interactions with the ads.

In the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland, a consent form from Google asks for your choice before any ad is requested. Elsewhere the game asks with its own window. Without your consent to personalised ads, only non-personalised ads are requested. You can reopen your ad choices under Settings > Privacy options. You can also reset or delete the advertising identifier in your device settings.

How Google uses data from apps that use its services: https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites


5. Who receives data

Google Ireland Limited / Google LLC, as the provider of Firebase Crashlytics, Firebase Remote Config, Google Analytics for Firebase and AdMob. Google may process data on servers outside your country, including the United States; it relies on the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework and standard contractual clauses. We do not sell your data and we share it with no one else.

Purchases: if you buy something in the shop, the payment is handled entirely by Google Play (or the App Store). We never see your card or payment details. The game only learns from the store which product was bought, and keeps the transaction identifier on your device so that a product is delivered once. "Restore purchases" in the shop asks the store again which one-time products your store account owns.

Rating window and our other games: the game may ask Google Play to show its own rating window, and Settings lists our other games with a link to their Google Play pages. Tapping a link opens Google Play. We send no data for either; the link only tells Google Play which of our games it was opened from. What you do in Google Play is covered by Google's privacy policy.


6. How long data is kept

Crash reports: 90 days. Play statistics: up to 14 months. Data on your device: until you delete the game or its data.


7. Your rights

Depending on where you live (for example under the GDPR, the UK GDPR or the Turkish Law No. 6698, KVKK), you have the right to ask what data is held about you, to have it corrected or deleted, to object to or restrict its use, to withdraw your consent at any time, and to complain to your data protection authority. Write to codingtechstudio@gmail.com; include your Data ID if the request is about play statistics. We answer within 30 days.


8. Permissions

Internet access (crash reports, game settings, statistics, ads), vibration (short feedback pulses you can switch off in Settings), the advertising identifier (ads), and billing (purchases through Google Play).


9. Changes

If this policy changes, the date at the top changes and the new text is published at the same address.


